/*
    We the best music, dj khalid
    System overview (brief):

    List a data structures and algorithms used:
        - A heap for the waiting list (holds patients waiting to be treated)
        - A hash table for the waiting room (holds patients and their assigned doctors)
        - A heap sort to print the current waiting list in order of highest to lowest priority
        - A circular buffer to hold the free, unasigned doctors


    Description of Inputs, Outputs, and system behaviour:
    The user flow:
        User is prompted to choose which operation they want to do (an integer for each option)
            If entering a new user (option 1), input:
                - Patient ID (positive integer)
                - Triage Level, the severity of the patient's status (positive integer)

                Then add patient is added to waiting list, or their position is updated if that ID is already registered.

                Outputs position in line if updated, or an error message if input was bad.
                
                Also, program checks if a doctor is available to assign the patient at the root to at this stage.

                Outputs a message confirming patient ID (int) was assigned a doctor ID (int), or a message indicating no doctors are available and patient ID (int) was added to list
        
            If discharging a patient from treatment room (option 2), input:
                - Patient ID (positive integer)

                Outputs an error message for bad input, an error message that no patient of the input ID (int) is currently being treated, or a confirmation that the patient of ID (int) was discharged and the doctor with unique ID (int) assigned to them is now free

                System automatically checks if there is a patient on the waiting list (since a doctor is free now),

                so also outputs a messaging confirming patient of ID (int) was assigned a doctor of ID (int), or a message saying the doctor is now on standby

            If viewing waiting list (option 3)
                No additional input, outputs the waiting list
                    - Position in line (integer)
                    - Patient ID (integer)
                    - Triage Level (integer)

            If viewing the waiting room (option 4)
                No additional input, outputs all patients being treated
                    - Patient ID (integer)
                    - Triage Level (integer)
                    - Doctor ID (integer)
            

            



*/